to-be-incorporated-into-paper-lines-64 = cons "The work is organized by a graph of tasks in the language (“How the workflow is held in the language today”, below). Its rules:" (cons "" (cons "**Nodes.**" (cons "- There is one kind of node. Its name is a well-formed English sentence saying what it is." (cons "- There are no tickets and no ticket numbers: an empty identifier such as a number exists nowhere." (cons "" (cons "**A node's children completely cover it.**" (cons "- A leaf is resolved when its work is done." (cons "- Any other node is resolved exactly when all its children are; there is no separate step for the" (cons "  parent." (cons "- If a node turns out not to be achieved by its children, a child is added at once, possibly as" (cons (quoted (cons "  broad as " (cons "determine and do everything else this needs" (cons "." nil)))) (cons "- A missed requirement refutes the belief that the breakdown was understood, so it calls for a" (cons "  residual of that kind, not a one-off item." (cons "- There is never scope that is unspecified, only further detail that is unspecified." (cons "" (cons "**Expansion only when work begins.**" (cons "- A node is broken into children exactly when one of them is to become active, so every internal" (cons "  node has a child that is active or complete." (cons "- Only a session that has taken the task on, with its full context, breaks it down." (cons "- A session passing by may add context to a task's statement, never subtasks." (cons "" (cons "**States.** A node is in progress or pending. There is one owner, Avik, and sessions hold no" (cons "identity. The graph lists the leaves in progress (`in-progress`) and the leaves resolved" (cons "(`resolved`); every other leaf is pending. A resolved leaf stays in the graph, since every internal" (cons "node has a child that is active or complete. A node with children is resolved exactly when all of" (cons "them are." (cons "" (cons "**Order.**" (cons "- There is no scalar priority, value, score or estimate. A node's value is what it serves, up to the" (cons (quoted (cons "  root, " (cons "Avik wants this" (cons "." nil)))) (cons "- Dependencies give every valid order. Enabling is conjunctive: work starts only when all its" (cons "  prerequisites are resolved." (cons "- Among work that can start, X supersedes Y when the waiting work X is a prerequisite of strictly" (cons "  contains Y's. Where neither contains the other, the graph expresses no preference." (cons "- A session states what the order forces. It does not choose a schedule of its own." (cons "" (cons "**Every top-level object of the code has a reason for existing,** either by being used or by its" (cons "statement of what it is part of." (cons "- Attachments go to the most specific node, and attaching high is treated like changing the org" (cons "  chart." (cons "- Higher levels are more visible, so attaching there uses a scarce commons." (cons "- A generator states the reason of each term it generates when it generates it." (cons "- A breakdown that is known exactly can be frozen, so nothing more is added there. Being unable to" (cons "  freeze it means the breakdown is not known." (cons "" (cons "**Findings at code sites.** A defect or gap found at a code site is either wrong, pointless to raise," (cons "or relevant to a goal. If it is relevant, it goes into that goal's statement." (cons "" (cons "**Documents attach to nodes** as essential context, by `document`, and the connection is exact or" (cons "absent. No comment convention stands in for it." (cons "" (cons "**No estimates and no research.**" (cons "- No size, duration or difficulty is ever stated. Everything left is trivial." (cons "- Avik holds every answer, so what a session does not see how to do is a question for Avik." (cons "" nil)))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
